# Commit after each change

When a task finishes with source or project-file edits, make a local git commit before you stop. Do not leave a dirty tree for later.

- Commit only what this change needs. One logical change, one commit.
- Do not push. Do not update git config. Do not skip hooks.
- Author stays `XueMusic <xuemusic@local>` via env or `git -c`, never `git config`.
- Do not commit secrets, APKs, `build/` installers, or empty `branding/`.
- If there is nothing to commit, say so. Do not create an empty commit.
